{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries","id":1264984,"title":"Semitic Covenants and Blood Sorceries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-06T09:04:42-08:00","id":1264984,"title":"Semitic Covenants and Blood Sorceries","content":"Hi guys! I'm new to VtR 2e and was wondering about anyone who would like to help or has ideas concerning Jewish and Semitic covenants and mystery cults. So far I have an outline for a Semitic pagan faction of CotC and a modern Jewish covenant. I can use some people to bounce some theology and culture with and blood sorcery as well as ideas for ancient and medieval covenants/cults. The focus is Jewish and Semitic pagan. I would also like some help with Hebrew, Arabic, Amharic, and a few other languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-12-2018, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T06:48:00-08:00","id":1265266,"title":"","content":"A comment first: generally modern Covenants are presented as cutting across cultural lines, however during Dark Eras there have been examples that were more geographically and culturally focused, primarily because they had distance between themselves and more inclusive competitors that gave them space to thrive. As the major Covenants evolved they hoovered up these more minor entities and they have become contemporarily forgotten. That's not to say X or Y vamp doesn't know of them--or even was a member at one point, just that they have re-invented themselves past that phase and it's irrelevant except for swapping a few tales and reminding themselves of boons owed or feuds unsettled. <br /> <br /> In the case of a Jewish-specific Covenant you have a people group who has worked very hard (with mixed success) to remain separate from others for thousands of years, propagating via natural methods as well as more rare conversion (Khazars, Ethiopians most notably). In these respects a &quot;Jewish&quot; Covenant has more grounds for modern survival than most, though do keep in mind that under CofD it could also function as a Mystery Cult (see: Mystery Cult Initiation Merit) very well, as it has all the trappings laid out for that. MCI would also make it easy for members to also belong to other Covenants, whereas the Jewish Covenant itself would semi-preclude deeper membership in say Invictus or whomever. Both approaches have historical analogues: Jewish figures as diligent integrators into mid- to high-social spheres, and Jewish figures as unrepentant social outcasts.<br /> <br /> Pick your own extent of conspiracy theories, by the way, keeping in mind that CofD is <b><i>NOT</i></b> real life and the game setting delights in mysteries and conspiracies driven by all manner of egregious human behavior (hence, &quot;darkness&quot;).<br /> <br /> Now a few questions you'll need to block things out:<br /> <br /> 1. When did it originate, and why? Covenants are normally a response to the question of vampiric existence, catalyzed by competing organizations. In this case, if you go back to the time of judges, let alone the first temple period, you'd have competition from the neighboring Great Covenant in Egypt, which could work.<br /> <br /> 2. What was the purpose of the Covenant, practically speaking? Is it like the Lancea, in which it attempts to explain the relationship between Yahweh (and Jewish strictures) and vampires? Or address practical (Carthian, Invictus) or mystical (Crone, Lancea, Ordo) aspects of their existence and interactions? Does it function as a self-defense and self-actualization league? (Legio Mortuus, Ordo)<br /> <br /> 3. What, if any, was the influence of the Assyrian diaspora? Similarly, the Babylonian diaspora? Even if you don't adopt &quot;lost tribe&quot; hypotheses (linking diasporic fragments to a variety of later peoples such as the Scythians/Cimmerians and beyond) embraced Jewish Covenant members in far-flung places would be easily left behind by rapid movements of their living relatives (torpor of course being a major factor). And... which other Covenants and traditions that were encountered, flavored the later, modern Jewish Covenant? <br /> <br /> 4. How did the Covenant handle the destruction(s) of the temple? This is effectively concurrent with #3, above, but includes the Roman destruction and diaspora. How does it handle the integration (or not) of mixed peoples with residency history in the same territories the Covenant claims? <br /> <br /> 5. What is/was the impact of Messianic mortal movements on the Covenant and its members? This points to Yeshua as the Christ-figure, but also the slew of competitor Messianics contemporary with the 1st century. Do you have sub-groups within the Covenant that view these and later figures differently? Is there a movement to search out and embrace such figures, to co-opt them as saviors of the Covenant versus the mortal tribes?<br /> <br /> 6. What was the impact of the Covenant on mortal (immortal?) persecutions during the first and second millennium by various religious factions (Roman Catholic and Islam, mainly and most widely)? This can include the Crusades. Bonus points for examining the impact of Mongol (Tengric) and Timur (Islamic) invasions on the region--note that these are one of the reasons Bagdad is not the world educational capital today.<br /> <br /> That ought to get you started....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T08:00:42-08:00","id":1265279,"title":"","content":"Also, as has been mentioned before, it may be prudent to learn about how Judaism at the time your covenant formed treats blood, corpses and living sacrifice. Blood is very powerful in Jewish history, being seen as the very essence of life. may have been in response to pagan semetic rituals, but I can't be sure. You're supposed to drain and salt away all the blood you can when you eat animals, as it is seen as not right to consume life that directly. Animal blood was used sparingly in Temple rituals according to the Torah, though. Some very important rituals, too. Human corpses and those who touch them were considered spiritually unclean in the past too, similarly to Shinto. That said, youwl don't have to say these guys ate somehow extra guilty about drinking blood, just remember that this is the cultural context within which your Jewish covenant may have been created.<br /> <br /> Also, Lilith. Whether they worship her or oppose her, she will probably have a big role in their mythos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-07-2018, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T08:17:07-08:00","id":1265285,"title":"","content":"I also think if you want to have vampire Jews or a Jewish covenant, they'd best fit as a sub-categorie of the Lancea et Sanctum, or an offshoot of the Lancea et Sanctum, or a mystery cult within the Lancea et Sanctum. The core book already states that while the Sanctum is often the dark mirror image of Christianity, often co-existing with their living Christian cousins, it's also perfectly possible to have a Jewish or Muslim Lancea et Sanctum, or a Lancea et Sanctum based on a mix of Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> I don't really see how Judaism fits in the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 11-07-2018, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:06:13-08:00","id":1265303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265285#post1265285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think if you want to have vampire Jews or a Jewish covenant, they'd best fit as a sub-categorie of the Lancea et Sanctum, or an offshoot of the Lancea et Sanctum, or a mystery cult within the Lancea et Sanctum. The core book already states that while the Sanctum is often the dark mirror image of Christianity, often co-existing with their living Christian cousins, it's also perfectly possible to have a Jewish or Muslim Lancea et Sanctum, or a Lancea et Sanctum based on a mix of Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> I don't really see how Judaism fits in the Circle of the Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well there are Judaic sorcery rumors going way back (Solomon especially, &quot;wisdom&quot; being associated with magic), so you can pick and choose what to work with. One of the reasons I posed the questions above is because a Judaic Covenant is going to be under pressure to fragment at various points, and bits of it (even, large bits) might gravitate away to join the superCovenants such as Lancea--but only after 400 when that group really got off the ground following the destruction of the Senex. <br /> <br /> I'll also tender that, were it to exist, Longinus might have been influenced in his philosophy by contact with an extant Judaic Covenant in the area of his ascension to vampirism. In that sense the eastern-Med side of the Lancea would have a pull toward an existing, philosophically similar Covenant. Negatives being that said Jewish Covenant could be generally insular and possibly already hammered by Rome much as the Great Covenant was broken. Note that Longinus eventually fled to Egypt and there found and founded the Lancea.<br /> <br /> By modern nights? There are quite a few decision points to be made along the way that could point toward how a Judaic Covenant might survive or not. If not, then surely its members would have found compatible homes within other Covenants--including the Lancea. However the point of the thread as posted is &quot;if it exists what could it be?&quot; So, let's respect that.<br /> <br /> Also, second the point that Lilith should figure into Covenant mythology strongly.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T20:56:25-08:00","id":1265441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the case of a Jewish-specific Covenant you have a people group who has worked very hard (with mixed success) to remain separate from others for thousands of years, propagating via natural methods as well as more rare conversion (Khazars, Ethiopians most notably).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The community in Ethiopia actually dates back to the time of King Solomon. Given that Haymanot Judaism is in a fair amount of circles considered closest to the ancient practice I'm thinking about definitely having them as a direct descendant of the ones that would've stalked the nights during the Biblical Era. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In these respects, a &quot;Jewish&quot; Covenant has more grounds for modern survival than most, though do keep in mind that under CofD it could also function as a Mystery Cult (see: Mystery Cult Initiation Merit) very well, as it has all the trappings laid out for that. MCI would also make it easy for members to also belong to other Covenants, whereas the Jewish Covenant itself would semi-preclude deeper membership in say Invictus or whomever. Both approaches have historical analogues: Jewish figures as diligent integrators into mid- to high-social spheres, and Jewish figures as unrepentant social outcasts.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Very true. Especially given hostilities from Kindred who were possibly antisemitic in life(Lancea et Sanctum has a group of Protestant white supremacists) it'd be wise to make it a Mystery Cult and it'd add some fun stuff. I'll likely have both that represent different regions. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. When did it originate, and why? Covenants are normally a response to the question of vampiric existence, catalyzed by competing organizations. In this case, if you go back to the time of judges, let alone the first temple period, you'd have competition from the neighboring Great Covenant in Egypt, which could work.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The earliest Judaic covenant I was thinking about was having one that goes back to the time of the First Temple. Each covenant and mystery cult would function differently to react to the varying climates they find themselves in with the consistency of community and people. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2. What was the purpose of the Covenant, practically speaking? Is it like the Lancea, in which it attempts to explain the relationship between Yahweh (and Jewish strictures) and vampires? Or address practical (Carthian, Invictus) or mystical (Crone, Lancea, Ordo) aspects of their existence and interactions? Does it function as a self-defense and self-actualization league? (Legio Mortuus, Ordo)</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Very true. I was thinking about it being based in a relationship with G-d and the living community of Jews. With a few variations.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">3. What, if any, was the influence of the Assyrian diaspora? Similarly, the Babylonian diaspora? Even if you don't adopt &quot;lost tribe&quot; hypotheses (linking diasporic fragments to a variety of later peoples such as the Scythians/Cimmerians and beyond) embraced Jewish Covenant members in far-flung places would be easily left behind by rapid movements of their living relatives (torpor, of course, is a major factor). And... which other Covenants and traditions that were encountered, flavored the later, modern Jewish Covenant?</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I thought of representing those mostly as mystery cults and it'd be interesting to see how their definition of self-shifts. So far I plan for Ethiopia, Morocco, Yemen, and Eretz Yisrael to be home to covenants and mystery cults that can trace themselves back long enough to rival Lancea et Sanctum. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">4. How did the Covenant handle the destruction(s) of the temple? This is effectively concurrent with #3, above, but includes the Roman destruction and diaspora. How does it handle the integration (or not) of mixed peoples with residency history in the same territories the Covenant claims?</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Depends on where they are. I was thinking about them being mystery cults during violent times and a normal covenant during times of calm. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">5. What is/was the impact of Messianic mortal movements on the Covenant and its members? This points to Yeshua as the Christ-figure, but also the slew of competitor Messianics contemporary with the 1st century. Do you have sub-groups within the Covenant that view these and later figures differently? Is there a movement to search out and embrace such figures, to co-opt them as saviors of the Covenant versus the mortal tribes?</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Definitely thinking about them having various sub-factions. The most common theme in my experience with Jewish tradition is an ethical and theological debate that causes separations on schools of thought. I have some ideas about Sicari, Pharisees, Nazarenes, and later Frankists and Hassids. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265266#post1265266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">6. What was the impact of the Covenant on mortal (immortal?) persecutions during the first and second millennium by various religious factions (Roman Catholic and Islam, mainly and most widely)? This can include the Crusades. Bonus points for examining the impact of Mongol (Tengric) and Timur (Islamic) invasions on the region--note that these are one of the reasons Bagdad is not the world educational capital today.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Very true. I was thinking about for the Khazars that Judaism and Tengri might mix(since only some elite converted to Judaism), probably a hidden group in most of Europe rarely numbering of 5-10, and in the Middle East blending ling I guess. Still working that region out since both formats fit. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-08-2018, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T21:02:14-08:00","id":1265444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265285#post1265285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think if you want to have vampire Jews or a Jewish covenant, they'd best fit as a sub-category of the Lancea et Sanctum, or an offshoot of the Lancea et Sanctum, or a mystery cult within the Lancea et Sanctum. The core book already states that while the Sanctum is often the dark mirror image of Christianity, often co-existing with their living Christian cousins, it's also perfectly possible to have a Jewish or Muslim Lancea et Sanctum, or a Lancea et Sanctum based on a mix of Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> I don't really see how Judaism fits in the Circle of the Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dammitic Creed is already part of Lancea et Sanctum. Due to religious differences that have led to violent antisemitism throughout history, I find it more likely that while some follow Longinus, those ones were originally a younger group who created a sub-faction. Likely Frankists who received the embrace. For those in relationship to Lilith(Dark Mother, Whore), especially looking at Kabbalistic and Talmudic works, they're actually more at home with Circle of the Crone or a Mystery Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-08-2018, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T21:04:37-08:00","id":1265445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265279#post1265279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as has been mentioned before, it may be prudent to learn about how Judaism at the time your covenant formed treats blood, corpses and living sacrifice. Blood is very powerful in Jewish history, is seen as the very essence of life. may have been in response to pagan Semitic rituals, but I can't be sure. You're supposed to drain and salt away all the blood you can when you eat animals, as it is seen as not right to consume life that directly. Animal blood was used sparingly in Temple rituals according to the Torah, though. Some very important rituals, too. Human corpses and those who touch them were considered spiritually unclean in the past too, similarly to Shinto. That said, you don't have to say these guys ate somehow extra guilty about drinking blood, just remember that this is the cultural context within which your Jewish covenant may have been created.<br /> <br /> Also, Lilith. Whether they worship her or oppose her, she will probably have a big role in their mythos</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about her being venerated by a matriarchial mystery cult that falls in with the Circle of the Crone. Their ideology might come closer to Lancea at certain points like tempting men to better them. Yeah. With the blood, I was thinking that a mystery cult might exist that makes them perceive themselves as closer to G-d since they are drinking what is usually reserved for G-d. By and large, I was going to make it so most try to abstain from feeding unless absolutely needed and they have stricter restrictions regarding on who to feed on, when, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-08-2018, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T23:39:30-08:00","id":1265456,"title":"","content":"According Requiem for Rome, during Roman Empire, the Lancea et Sanctum was originally a small Jewish faction (the Sanctum) of the Peregrine Collegia, a Wing from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Around 1st century, they oponed their ranks to other faiths, as Christians or Gnostics. Around third or fourth century, the followers of Longinos (the Sanctum) had become the dominant faction of this group, and splintered from the Peregrine College to create their own Wing (or Covenant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T03:19:46-08:00","id":1265469,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144\" target=\"_blank\">This is one of the funnier discussions relevant to Jewish Vampires.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T04:50:28-08:00","id":1265481,"title":"","content":"Remember that all covenants need a dark side. Joining a covenant is a Humanity breaking point. And just like mortal Christian theologists would be disgusted by the practices of the Sanctum, you can make a Jewish covenant a perversion of what is held sacred by the Jewish people.<br /> <br /> For an example, here is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> 's homebrew Hunter Conspiracy: the Cage of Shadows. Its not a Covenant, but it is very vampire-focused and blood-themed. Fair warning, they will feel very viscerally -wrong-, especially to those who know exactly which traditions they are perverting<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/407911-hunter-cult-cage-of-shadows\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/407911-hunter-cult-cage-of-shadows\"> Hunter-Cult: Cage of Shadows - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/407911-hunter-cult-cage-of-shadows\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/407911-hunter-cult-cage-of-shadows </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Cage of Shadows Caretakers of the Dark Mother [a black owl locked inside a thorny cage] It is said that every religion has its heresy. Actually, most of the time </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:00:41-08:00","id":1265645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265456#post1265456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Requiem for Rome, during the Roman Empire, the Lancea et Sanctum was originally a small Jewish faction (the Sanctum) of the Peregrine Collegia, a Wing from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Around 1st century, they opened their ranks to other faiths, as Christians or Gnostics. Around third or fourth century, the followers of Longinus (the Sanctum) had become the dominant faction of this group and splintered from the Peregrine College to create their own Wing (or Covenant).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I'll expand and make the pre-Longinian group more like a mystery cult given Jewish-Roman relations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:03:02-08:00","id":1265646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265469#post1265469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144\" target=\"_blank\">This is one of the funnier discussions relevant to Jewish Vampires.</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Hahaha!! I remember this from my old Jumblr(Jewish Tumblr) days! Thank you very much! It definitely gives a fair deal of more liberty to ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:07:39-08:00","id":1265647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265481#post1265481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that all covenants need a dark side. Joining a covenant is a Humanity breaking point. And just like mortal Christian theologists would be disgusted by the practices of the Sanctum, you can make a Jewish covenant a perversion of what is held sacred by the Jewish people.<br /> <br /> For an example, here is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> 's homebrew Hunter Conspiracy: the Cage of Shadows. Its not a Covenant, but it is very vampire-focused and blood-themed. Fair warning, they will feel very viscerally -wrong-, especially to those who know exactly which traditions they are perverting<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/407911-hunter-cult-cage-of-shadows\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...age-of-shadows</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! I'm a fan and was thinking about one of the mystery cults being similar. I definitely agree that in some respects it should be a perversion, but I think that it will be in varying degress for each cult and covenant. I do assure you none are exactly &quot;good&quot;. The overall theme that each will have in common will likely be a sense of kinship with their living relatives, not unlike the Ravnos from VtM if I recollect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:17:33-08:00","id":1265649,"title":"","content":"Oh. I'm not the writer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:24:53-08:00","id":1265650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265649#post1265649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. I'm not the writer</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand! I've spoken to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> and their stuff is among my inspirations and a constant at my HtV games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T19:28:48-08:00","id":1265651,"title":"","content":"Ah. Cool. I'm a big fan of him too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:31:56-08:00","id":1265978,"title":"","content":"I think there was something in the Lancea Sanctum book about a jewish kabbalistic branch called Dammitic Creed or something like that.<br /> Remember mixing them with the Qedeshah (from Bloodlines: the Hidden) to form a splinter faction in my game's city in a game a few years aago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T14:35:34-08:00","id":1266496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1265978#post1265978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was something in the Lancea Sanctum book about a Jewish kabbalistic branch called Dammitic Creed or something like that.<br /> Remember mixing them with the Qedeshah (from Bloodlines: the Hidden) to form a splinter faction in my game's city in a game a few years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but in 2e it seems Lancea et Sanctum is more ex-Christian geared and the actual teachings of the sect and the likely history of antisemitism, I think it makes sense for in modern times for there to be a separate Jewish covenant as well as Jewish covenants/mystery cults throughout the history of the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:00:43-08:00","id":1266511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266496#post1266496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but in 2e it seems Lancea et Sanctum is more ex-Christian geared and the actual teachings of the sect and the likely history of antisemitism, I think it makes sense for in modern times for there to be a separate Jewish covenant as well as Jewish covenants/mystery cults throughout the history of the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing inherently Christian about the Lancea et Sanctum that can't easily be reskinned to fit Judaism, even in 2e.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum's main thing is that they believe their vampiric curse to be part of God's divine plan, to have vampires act as tempters, to test the faith of the mortal population (similar to Satan's role in the story of Job, which is an old Testament story by the way and also part of the Jewish Torah). That particular belief is not exclusive to Christianity. Islamic vampires and Jewish vampires can fit in that mold easily as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T18:47:20-08:00","id":1266571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266511#post1266511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's nothing inherently Christian about the Lancea et Sanctum that can't easily be reskinned to fit Judaism, even in 2e.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum's main thing is that they believe their vampiric curse to be part of God's divine plan, to have vampires act as tempters, to test the faith of the mortal population (similar to Satan's role in the story of Job, which is an old Testament story by the way and also part of the Jewish Torah). That particular belief is not exclusive to Christianity. Islamic vampires and Jewish vampires can fit in that mold easily as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and the Dammitic and Iblic Creeds are fine, but to take rich cultures and histories and water them down because they're Abrahamic is kinda lazy and a huge oversight. HaSatan is not a consistent enough theme in Judaism for ALL of them to fit into it. The Jewish Tanakh and the Christian Old Testament are different books due to the Christians including works considered apocryphal by Jews the message of both ultimately being different. In all honesty being &quot;G-d's Monsters&quot; works with some strains of Judaism but given the evolution of Jewish theology, it isn't exactly compatible entirely since the ultimate source of ethical behavior isn't meant to stem from a fear of damnation. Given the simple fact that Lancea is still largely a twisted mirror of Chalcedonian Christianity and their ranks are overwhelmingly full of ex-Christians who throughout history would likely have antisemitic behaviors that would make it necessary for Jewish covenants to still exist given that according to lore the Dammitic Creed wouldn't exist until the 1800's and even in the modern nights the literally have a white supremacist sect. Jewish mystery cults and covenants to represent the fullness of the diversity of the people is frankly just a good additive that books like Dark Eras do a pretty good job at opening the conversation for. That being said it should be noted for all of the Abrahamic faiths it's restrictive, but especially for Judaism and Islam given that they're not just slightly different from Christians, but entirely different religions with actual sects, schisms, and histories and this is nodded to due to the fact that the Iblic and Dammitic Creeds are both formed within the last three centuries. In terms of religions for humans, not that long, and in terms of neigh immortal elders who survived events ranging from the Crusades to Spanish Inquisition, not that long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T04:02:37-08:00","id":1266661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266571#post1266571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, and the Dammitic and Iblic Creeds are fine, but to take rich cultures and histories and water them down because they're Abrahamic is kinda lazy and a huge oversight. HaSatan is not a consistent enough theme in Judaism for ALL of them to fit into it. The Jewish Tanakh and the Christian Old Testament are different books due to the Christians including works considered apocryphal by Jews the message of both ultimately being different. In all honesty being &quot;G-d's Monsters&quot; works with some strains of Judaism but given the evolution of Jewish theology, it isn't exactly compatible entirely since the ultimate source of ethical behavior isn't meant to stem from a fear of damnation. Given the simple fact that Lancea is still largely a twisted mirror of Chalcedonian Christianity and their ranks are overwhelmingly full of ex-Christians who throughout history would likely have antisemitic behaviors that would make it necessary for Jewish covenants to still exist given that according to lore the Dammitic Creed wouldn't exist until the 1800's and even in the modern nights the literally have a white supremacist sect. Jewish mystery cults and covenants to represent the fullness of the diversity of the people is frankly just a good additive that books like Dark Eras do a pretty good job at opening the conversation for. That being said it should be noted for all of the Abrahamic faiths it's restrictive, but especially for Judaism and Islam given that they're not just slightly different from Christians, but entirely different religions with actual sects, schisms, and histories and this is nodded to due to the fact that the Iblic and Dammitic Creeds are both formed within the last three centuries. In terms of religions for humans, not that long, and in terms of neigh immortal elders who survived events ranging from the Crusades to Spanish Inquisition, not that long.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, it's not enough to close the issue. But can be a starting point to improvise/improve from to pique the interest of a ST that's just starting to delve into the subject.<br /> The specific conceit of them as actual branches of the LS tends to be mostly ignored in my experience anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T05:39:45-08:00","id":1266673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266661#post1266661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, it's not enough to close the issue. But can be a starting point to improvise/improve from to pique the interest of an ST that's just starting to delve into the subject.<br /> The specific concept of them as actual branches of the LS tends to be mostly ignored in my experience anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about the Dammitic Creed being formed by a splinter cell of ex-Frankists(a real Jewish heresy) from an Ashkenazi based covenant. They would exist around the time the lore states the first induction of the Dammitics and would be closest in ideas that would make it so they would be inducted. They'd likely start as a mystery cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T06:15:00-08:00","id":1266677,"title":"","content":"Ex because they decided that instead of transgression being its own virtue, it is a virtue when it is used by the already forsaken to help others stay on the righteous path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T06:30:12-08:00","id":1266680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266673#post1266673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about the Dammitic Creed being formed by a splinter cell of ex-Frankists(a real Jewish heresy) from an Ashkenazi based covenant. They would exist around the time the lore states the first induction of the Dammitics and would be closest in ideas that would make it so they would be inducted. They'd likely start as a mystery cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the older books, Bloodlines: the Hidden, has the Qedeshah, a bloodline of &quot;mothers of kindred&quot; that claims to have originated among hebrew women in Judea, amidst a context of worship of the Shekhinah as the second, feminine \u201chalf\u201d of G'd, what makes them also good fodder as members of the Dammitic Creed, another mystery cult, a syncretic branch with connections to the Crone or even all of the above.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thought of mentioning them as an interesting addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:42:51-08:00","id":1266709,"title":"","content":"I think that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a>'s comment was that you could mechanically reuse the Lancea, not that the Abrahamic origins made it appropriate to dump the three major religions and various minor sects with millions of theological man-hours behind them into one convenient bucket. <br /> <br /> And to reinforce the point, Lancea is the Covenant that helps define a vamp's relationship with a higher moral authority. (Circle cults help define her relationship with pseudo-peer if perhaps more powerful divinity figures/self.) A Jewish-centric Covenant or mystery cult will have a similar role, or it's not really more than a social club. There are other Covenants that serve as clubs better, and wield mystical power stemming from that role.<br /> <br /> To me, one of the key systemic factors in the exercise of Judaic religion is the expression of separation through purity. The avoidance of certain things or practice of them served to draw a line between the Jewish people and their neighbors, with the purpose of ensuring they remain distinct, hold intact the story of Yaweh's interactions with them as a group, and enable the Messiah to clearly trace lineage back to Abraham of the promise. The Levites were further separated and purified as a group and individually so they could serve as intermediaries in ways that would literally kill less-pure people.<br /> <br /> I'm certain I'm oversimplifying, and don't wish to argue the broad points, but this framework could help assign a suitable role for Jewish vamps: not as tempters of the flock, but as vicious watchdogs of its purity in ways even the priestly caste could not. They might draw significant inspiration from the story of Phinehas (Numbers 25, do not know Torah reference), who violently purified a key transgressor of the non-fraternization strictures, saving the people as a whole from a judgement plague that had killed 24,000 already. Interestingly, the promise to Phinehas went along the lines of (again, Bible not Torah excerpt) &quot;Now tell him that I [Yaweh] am making my special covenant of peace with him. In this covenant, I give him and his descendants a permanent right to the priesthood, for in his zeal for me, his G-d, he purified the people of Israel, making them right with me.&quot; (Note that in the remainder of the passage the instructions on what to do to the peoples who tempted Israel to worship Baal in this incident, through intermarriages was... thorough.)<br /> <br /> Now historically speaking we can assume a &quot;permanent right&quot; ends with death, but CofD being what it is, perhaps permanent is permanent? Or, at least argued as such by those for whose interest it serves.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:48:31-08:00","id":1266712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266677#post1266677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ex because they decided that instead of transgression being its own virtue, it is a virtue when it is used by the already forsaken to help others stay on the righteous path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex because the living Frankists would've died out and neither Jacob or Eva were actual messiahs. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:58:51-08:00","id":1266714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266709#post1266709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm certain I'm oversimplifying, and don't wish to argue the broad points, but this framework could help assign a suitable role for Jewish vamps: not as tempters of the flock, but as vicious watchdogs of its purity in ways, even the priestly caste could not. They might draw significant inspiration from the story of Phinehas (Numbers 25, do not know Torah reference), who violently purified a key transgressor of the non-fraternization strictures, saving the people as a whole from a judgment plague that had killed 24,000 already. Interestingly, the promise to Phinehas went along the lines of (again, Bible not Torah excerpt) &quot;Now tell him that I [Yaweh] am making my special covenant of peace with him. In this covenant, I give him and his descendants a permanent right to the priesthood, for in his zeal for me, his G-d, he purified the people of Israel, making them right with me.&quot; (Note that in the remainder of the passage the instructions on what to do to the peoples who tempted Israel to worship Baal in this incident, through intermarriages was... thorough.)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">True. That is definitely the vein that I'm trying to keep consistent with all of the small groups. A more sense of defending than persecuting given the different historical and theological divisions and that being a more solid consistency. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:10:18-08:00","id":1266729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266714#post1266714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">True. That is definitely the vein that I'm trying to keep consistent with all of the small groups. A more sense of defending than persecuting given the different historical and theological divisions and that being a more solid consistency. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that Jewish culture pre-Roman diaspora has been typified by periods of drifting theological practice punctuated by extended purges and cleansings, you could reflect on the effects of torpor on the &quot;flock&quot; and the measures needed to excise rot in the flock once the most zealous awaken. As an example, certainly the story of the Exodus is typified by &quot;this is what it takes to kill impure behavior in a body politic--with fire!&quot;<br /> <br /> Modern cultural sensibilities don't align well with that, but if you really, really absolutely have to make the policeman in people's heads effective, then massive and obviously deadly, swift punishment is the only way to go....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T11:03:55-08:00","id":1266737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266571#post1266571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, and the Dammitic and Iblic Creeds are fine, but to take rich cultures and histories and water them down because they're Abrahamic is kinda lazy and a huge oversight. HaSatan is not a consistent enough theme in Judaism for ALL of them to fit into it. The Jewish Tanakh and the Christian Old Testament are different books due to the Christians including works considered apocryphal by Jews the message of both ultimately being different. In all honesty being &quot;G-d's Monsters&quot; works with some strains of Judaism but given the evolution of Jewish theology, it isn't exactly compatible entirely since the ultimate source of ethical behavior isn't meant to stem from a fear of damnation. Given the simple fact that Lancea is still largely a twisted mirror of Chalcedonian Christianity and their ranks are overwhelmingly full of ex-Christians who throughout history would likely have antisemitic behaviors that would make it necessary for Jewish covenants to still exist given that according to lore the Dammitic Creed wouldn't exist until the 1800's and even in the modern nights the literally have a white supremacist sect. Jewish mystery cults and covenants to represent the fullness of the diversity of the people is frankly just a good additive that books like Dark Eras do a pretty good job at opening the conversation for. That being said it should be noted for all of the Abrahamic faiths it's restrictive, but especially for Judaism and Islam given that they're not just slightly different from Christians, but entirely different religions with actual sects, schisms, and histories and this is nodded to due to the fact that the Iblic and Dammitic Creeds are both formed within the last three centuries. In terms of religions for humans, not that long, and in terms of neigh immortal elders who survived events ranging from the Crusades to Spanish Inquisition, not that long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampire the Requiem is a game, not a theology lecture. So of course it's going to be dumbed down. If you and your players want to turn your games into a theology lesson, then by all means, it certainly isn't my intention to tell you how to run/play your games. But the average player isn't going to care about any of the nuance you just brought up. Especially because the Lancea et Sanctum isn't any of these religions.<br /> <br /> I think that's the most important thing to understand. The Sanctum <b><i>isn't</i></b> Christian. The Sanctum also isn't Jewish, nor Islamic. The Sanctum is its own religion, it's a new religion created specifically for the Damned, because quite frankly Christianity, Judaism and Islam doesn't apply to them (those religion apply to mortals, not to the undead Damned, who's state of being is arguably inherently incompatible with Christianity, Judaism and Islam). The Sanctum's creed appeals to ex-Christian vampires, ex-Jewish vampires and ex-Muslim vampires. That at least was the intention of the writers. The Lancea et Sanctum was never supposed to be exclusively ex-Christian. And if you want your version of the Sanctum in your game to fit a specific type of ex-Jews, you can easily reskin the Sanctum to fit your needs. The core of the Sanctum is being God's monsters to test the faith of the mortal population. That doesn't necessarily mean a Sanctified has to <i>scare</i> mortals into being proper Christians/Jews/Muslims, quite the contrary. It simply means they test how strong a mortal's faith in God is, and whether they'll stay on the straight and narrow even when tempted by evil. If you're familiar with the story of Job you'd understand that fear (of God) has absolutely nothing to do with this.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> was right, even if you disagree with what I just wrote, the point still stands that from at least a game-mechanics perspective, the Lancea et Sanctum is very compatible with Judaism. Just rewrite the lore but keep (most of) the Sanctum merits and Theban Sorcery. That should easily be doable, at the very least it's an easier and more logical fit than trying to reskin Cruac and the Crone merits to fit your Jewish ideology. That's just my opinion though. If you think Cruac is easier to rework into your homebrew Jewish covenant, then by all means, go for it. But you asked for ideas and advice, so here I am, advising to use the Lancea et Sanctum stuff as a basis for your Jewish covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 11-12-2018, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T13:52:42-08:00","id":1266780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266737#post1266737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampire the Requiem is a game, not a theology lecture. So, of course, it's going to be dumbed down. If you and your players want to turn your games into a theology lesson, then, by all means, it certainly isn't my intention to tell you how to run/play your games. But the average player isn't going to care about any of the nuances you just brought up. Especially because the Lancea et Sanctum isn't any of these religions.<br /> <br /> I think that's the most important thing to understand. The Sanctum <b><i>isn't</i></b> Christian. The Sanctum also isn't Jewish, nor Islamic. The Sanctum is its own religion, it's a new religion created specifically for the Damned, because quite frankly Christianity, Judaism, and Islam doesn't apply to them (those religions apply to mortals, not to the undead Damned, whose state of being is arguably inherently incompatible with Christianity, Judaism, and Islam). The Sanctum's creed appeals to ex-Christian vampires, ex-Jewish vampires, and ex-Muslim vampires. That at least was the intention of the writers. The Lancea et Sanctum was never supposed to be exclusively ex-Christian. And if you want your version of the Sanctum in your game to fit a specific type of ex-Jews, you can easily reskin the Sanctum to fit your needs. The core of the Sanctum is being God's monsters to test the faith of the mortal population. That doesn't necessarily mean a Sanctified has to <i>scare</i> mortals into being proper Christians/Jews/Muslims, quite the contrary. It simply means they test how strong a mortal's faith in God is, and whether they'll stay on the straight and narrow even when tempted by evil. If you're familiar with the story of Job you'd understand that fear (of God) has absolutely nothing to do with this.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> was right, even if you disagree with what I just wrote, the point still stands that from at least a game mechanics perspective, the Lancea et Sanctum is very compatible with Judaism. Just rewrite the lore but keep (most of) the Sanctum merits and Theban Sorcery. That should easily be doable, at the very least it's an easier and more logical fit than trying to reskin Cruac and the Crone merits to fit your Jewish ideology. That's just my opinion though. If you think Cruac is easier to rework into your homebrew Jewish covenant, then, by all means, go for it. But you asked for ideas and advice, so here I am, advising to use the Lancea et Sanctum stuff as a basis for your Jewish covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Didn't mean to sound like a jerk if I did earlier. It's just that my aim is to take into consideration a variety of nuance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T19:38:20-08:00","id":1266845,"title":"","content":"If any of you are interested I can link the Google Docs that has the assortment of the cults and covenants in development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T19:54:48-08:00","id":1266848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266737#post1266737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> was right, even if you disagree with what I just wrote, the point still stands that from at least a game-mechanics perspective, the Lancea et Sanctum is very compatible with Judaism. Just rewrite the lore but keep (most of) the Sanctum merits and Theban Sorcery. That should easily be doable, at the very least it's an easier and more logical fit than trying to reskin Cruac and the Crone merits to fit your Jewish ideology. That's just my opinion though. If you think Cruac is easier to rework into your homebrew Jewish covenant, then by all means, go for it. But you asked for ideas and advice, so here I am, advising to use the Lancea et Sanctum stuff as a basis for your Jewish covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd reskin Lancea with a fresh coat of pseudo-religious paint to mesh with Judaic practices and take a subset of Theban Sorcery based on handwaving some kind of association with the Key of Solomon, first Temple and the king's library of wisdom. Maybe focus on the binding of unclean spirits or somesuch. Mix in heretical factions that swerve toward Lilithian interpretations justifying why monsters are permitted to harass mankind. <br /> <br /> Look, you can do Lancea as a separate religious movement tailored to the needs of the long-dead, or something locally current to the practices of bloodsuckers who are still looking over their eternal shoulders for hellfire, so to speak. It will, however, forever consist of individuals who come with their own experiences and beliefs, trying to make sense of a god (lowercase on purpose) who abandoned them to the night--or not. VtR is still a personal horror game, so the real question is: what is going to most resonate with your table and create the greatest dissonance between terrible and comforting?<br /> <br /> Do what makes sense for the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:35:55-08:00","id":1266965,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is relevant, but are you playing with a majority Jewish table? Have they expressed interest in exploring the concept of religious vampires outside the existing neo-pagan, Heretical Christian and maltheistic covenants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T18:15:14-08:00","id":1267154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1266965#post1266965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is relevant, but are you playing with a majority Jewish table? Have they expressed interest in exploring the concept of religious vampires outside the existing neo-pagan, Heretical Christian, and maltheistic covenants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually making this for a group of friends I play with at my Hillel who have a solid interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-13-2018, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T18:17:42-08:00","id":1267155,"title":"","content":"Here is the first that will be founded during the Israelite Era:<ul><li>Rephaim(Mystery Cult)<ul><li>History: During the long nights of the following Exodus out of Egypt, the Israelites were not the only ones to make an escape from slavery. Amongst the tribes hid a small group of Kindred. Little is known of these early Israelite Kindred before one by the name of Yitzhak of Dan united them. He taught that they were meant to keep the people from the temptations of the other nations. Dark protectors that when the people strayed, they wreaked havoc. They fought against threats presented by mundane and supernatural foes. The group more or less disappeared by the time of the Babylonian Captivity, by then the faith shifting from henotheistic and monlatristic, to monotheistic, though similar groups will appear later in history.</li> <li>Beliefs: While El and Asherah are supreme, they are no longer our patrons. We serve Maweth and Resheph foremost, for our condition is a covenant with them.</li> <li>Rituals and Observances:<ul><li>Mikvah at Gehenna: The newly embraced must bathe in the blood of slaughtered animals in a twist of the sin offerings. This occurs once a year every Yom Kippur.</li> <li>Abstain from contact with Levites or Kohanim.</li> </ul></li> <li>Status:<ul><li>Newly embraced, survival is difficult in an environment that offers little shelter and is full of enemies. They gain Survival Specialty in Hiding.</li> <li>It\u2019s a lethal world for everyone during this time and you know the ropes around the small domain you\u2019ve cut out for yourself. Because of this, you gain the Direction Sense merit free of charge.</li> <li>You\u2019ve been around for some time and know how to tell when something is awry. You gain the Danger Sense merit free of charge.</li> <li>At this point, you\u2019ve been around long enough and have come to know of the others the Maweth is a steward over. You gain the Medium merit free of charge.</li> <li>The highest ranking of the Rephaim are master survivors and warriors. Those who make it this far gain four dots that can be spent in Retainers or Allies.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","user":"Spectre9924","date":". 11-13-2018, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:07:07-08:00","id":1267170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267155#post1267155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the first that will be founded during the Israelite Era:[LIST][*]Rephaim(Mystery Cult)[LIST][*]History: During the long nights of the following Exodus out of Egypt, the Israelites were not the only ones to make an escape from slavery. Amongst the tribes hid a small group of Kindred. Little is known of these early Israelite Kindred before one by the name of Yitzhak of Dan united them. He taught that they were meant to keep the people from the temptations of the other nations. Dark protectors that when the people strayed, they wreaked havoc. They fought against threats presented by mundane and supernatural foes. The group more or less disappeared by the time of the Babylonian Captivity, by then the faith shifting from henotheistic and monlatristic, to monotheistic, though similar groups will appear later in history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I bet there' some interesting encounters there, in the process out of Egypt. Hmm. Wonder who it was who confronted Moses' family on the way in, whom Zipporah placated with a circumcised blood offering, eh?<br /> <br /> So here you're linking back to a figure we could assume was embraced in Egypt, from among the sojourning Israelites in the 400-year stay. So a member we would assume of the long-lived Great Covenant, and devoted filially to the protection of the living in Goshen--who we can understand were well-regarded in Egypt for a long time. Interesting.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:34:27-08:00","id":1267177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267170#post1267170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I bet there' some interesting encounters there, in the process out of Egypt. Hmm. Wonder who it was who confronted Moses' family on the way in, whom Zipporah placated with a circumcised blood offering, eh?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! Possibly even ghoul families establishing a relationship through that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267170#post1267170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So here you're linking back to a figure we could assume was embraced in Egypt, from among the sojourning Israelites in the 400-year stay. So a member we would assume of the long-lived Great Covenant, and devoted filially to the protection of the living in Goshen--who we can understand were well-regarded in Egypt for a long time. Interesting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very likely. They would've been at least embraced by likely a Nosferatu, Gangrel, or Daeva member. I'm thinking about the way to create Ov and Yidoni as a blood sorcery. Whether to use Cruac or create something using &quot;sacraments and blasphemies&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T04:25:55-08:00","id":1267252,"title":"","content":"I love this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T06:20:54-08:00","id":1267269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267177#post1267177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very likely. They would've been at least embraced by likely a Nosferatu, Gangrel, or Daeva member. I'm thinking about the way to create Ov and Yidoni as a blood sorcery. Whether to use Cruac or create something using &quot;sacraments and blasphemies&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the clan books the Daeva had a strong presence in the near-east, while the Mekhet were firmly Egyptian. Both Nos and Mekhet would work very well as shadows to the living tribes, especially in an environment of semi-nomadic tent-dwellers. Gangrel could work as well of course, with the obvious advantages of Protean. <br /> <br /> Since you're basing the most codified origins back to Egypt (which is highly defensible), it would make most sense to adapt Theban using sacraments and blasphemies. One angle to possibly take is to highlight the role the vamps decided to take as instruments of divine will and judgement--a channel for what Yahweh said He was going to do; thus, they used their powers to accomplish miraculous things such as summoning plagues and smaller-scale disasters. Not supplanting the divine guidance provided to the tribes, but supplementing it as agents. In that case Theban is closer to what you want since Cruac is more focused on personal &quot;be the god&quot; kind of expressions (but not entirely of course).<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T21:42:16-08:00","id":1267502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267269#post1267269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on the clan books the Daeva had a strong presence in the near-east, while the Mekhet were firmly Egyptian. Both Nos and Mekhet would work very well as shadows to the living tribes, especially in an environment of semi-nomadic tent-dwellers. Gangrel could work as well of course, with the obvious advantages of Protean.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! I was thinking about them being mostly Nosferatu and Gangrel with some Daeva and even less Mekhet(if any).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267269#post1267269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since you're basing the most codified origins back to Egypt (which is highly defensible), it would make </span></span></span>the most<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> sense to adapt Theban using sacraments and blasphemies. One angle to possibly take is to highlight the role the vamps decided to take as instruments of divine will and </span></span></span>judgment<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">--a channel for what YHWH said He was going to do; thus, they used their powers to accomplish miraculous things such as summoning plagues and smaller-scale disasters. Not supplanting the divine guidance provided to the tribes, but supplementing it as agents. In that </span></span></span>case<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, Theban is closer to what you want since Cruac is more focused on personal &quot;be the god&quot; kind of expressions (but not entirely of course).</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I see what you mean. I was thinking of having Ov and Yidoni closer to Cruac to kinda fit the bloody rites they already commit in honor of Resheph and Maweth. I was going to have Hekhalot be a system like Theban to highlight the cultural and theological shift.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T21:53:21-08:00","id":1267504,"title":"","content":"Is the theme system from &quot;sacraments and blasphemies&quot; usable in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T00:02:57-08:00","id":1267782,"title":"","content":"Mmmostly?<br /> <br /> The sample Blood Sorceries in the 2e core were designed using Sacraments and Blasphemies as a partial reference IIRC, so with a couple tweaks for things like time per roll and Experience cost per dot of a Theme they should work basically fine. Ooon that note of intervals though, I don't have my books up right now but I'm 99% sure 2e sorceries use much longer intervals than S&amp;B did... it'd probably be good to change one or the other for consistency's sake, or change both to somewhere between the two if you feel one interval or the other would be too fast or too slow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-16-2018, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T03:44:37-08:00","id":1267796,"title":"","content":"2e Blood Sorceries takes ages to perform. There is a sidebar in 2e core on page 151 that says that you can use the themes from the Blood Sorcery book. It just says to replace the old ritual extended action with that of the 2e version. As far as I know BS Themes are fully compatible (and actually listed alongside regular dot ratings for rituals in 2e supplements) with the tiny exception that they forgot to mention how much Theme dots should cost when bought separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:56:31-08:00","id":1268938,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Ov and Yidoni(Cruac):<ul><li>History: The covenant of Resheph and Maweth bestows a mere inkling of their power upon you. Sarai of Benjamin was the first to be revealed this dark secret. As the first childe of Yitzhak, she was charged with learning the secrets of the blood. It is said that the first she taught who learned mastery completed it upon the night of Moses\u2019s death. Only a few were permitted to know and study at a time, for the secrets that this revealed could cause cruelty in those without a strong connection to the world and calling.</li> <li>Learning: Because each dot is a breaking point for Humanity 4 and higher, simply knowing caps Humanity at 10 - dots. If a character increases his Ov and Yidoni score higher than his Humanity would normally allow, his Humanity immediately drops to the appropriate level and he is considered to have rolled a Dramatic Failure on the detachment test.</li> <li>Mechanics:<ul><li>Linked Themes: Creation and Protection</li> <li>Sacrifice: All rituals cost one Vitae per dot in the highest Theme of the rite. The first Vitae is absorbed by the caster as though fuelling a Discipline. Any remaining Vitae used must leave the ritualist's body and be used in the ritual's casting, usually by means of a self-inflicted wound.</li> <li>Dice Pools:<ul><li>Improvised: Manipulation + Occult + Theme</li> <li>Creation: Composure + Crafts + Creation</li> <li>Destruction: Presence + Athletics + Destruction</li> <li>Divination: Composure + Investigation + Divination</li> <li>Protection: Presence + Stealth + Protection</li> <li>Transmutation: Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Motifs:<ul><li>Israelite: \u200bRituals often involve symbolic slaughter, colorful vestments, golden adornments, braziers issuing odd-colored smoke, altars and the like, and imprecations to the powers of Israelite or Canaanite deities, particularly to Resheph and, of course, to Maweth. An air of holy mystery covers the ritualist.</li> <li>Occult: Students of the art spent much of their time learning at the side of an experienced practitioner in solitude for years. The rites themselves include an extreme precision and the study of an assortment of the otherworldly that are taken into account.</li> <li>Corrupting: The touch of pestilence and death degrades and putrifies what it touches. Dedicated practitioners have a battered soul and hailed with a special respect for being able to still withstand. As the blood settles it becomes inert and impotent. The area feels deaded.</li> </ul></li> <li>Rituals:<ul><li>Rousing of the Others(Transmutation 1)<ul><li>Description: This ritual targets a location where the borders between the real world and the place of spirits and ghosts are thin, such as a graveyard or a house where a murder has been committed. The ritualist increases the supernatural ambiance of the place, which manifests in effects such as a sudden chill, witch-fire playing around the trees, apparitions flickering in people's peripheral vision, or rot and molds spontaneously appearing.</li> <li>Effect: All Social dice pools are penalized by the ritual's Potency, apart from Intimidation which instead gains a corresponding bonus.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Area of Effect, Duration, and Potency.</li> <li>Resisted: Resolve</li> </ul></li> <li>Eyes of the Multitude(Divination 2)<ul><li>Description: The ritualist physically touches the target during the ritual. The chosen celebrant becomes the eyes and ears of the ritualist.</li> <li>Effect: For the rest of the night, the ritualist may see and hear what the subject does, no matter the distance.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Duration</li> <li>Contested: Composure</li> </ul></li> <li>Culling of Resheph(Creation 2)<ul><li>Description: Your covenant is with plague and death. The ritualist brings about the purview of their dark patron and inflicts the area with their power.</li> <li>Effect: The ritualist summons a disease to infect the local population.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Range and Radius</li> </ul></li> <li>Walk with the Others(Divination 2)<ul><li>Description: Death is common in these lands. Part of your covenant is to be a shepherd of the dead. The ritualist learns how to take a glimpse into the world beside our own.</li> <li>Effect: The ritualist gains the ability to question the dead in the area.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Duration</li> </ul></li> <li>Flesh of Cedar(Protection 3)<ul><li>Description: The ritualist wards themselves against being impaled through the heart.</li> <li>Effect: Attempts to stake fail until sunrise.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Duration</li> </ul></li> <li>Will of our Ancestors(Protection 4)<ul><li>Description: The ritualist makes themselves immune to sways of another\u2019s blood.</li> <li>Effect: The ritualist makes themselves immune to Vinculum and blood addiction. This doesn\u2019t counteract anything previously obtained.</li> <li>Common Ritual Factors: Duration</li> </ul></li> <li>Opening Sheol(Divination 5, Transmutation 4)<ul><li>Description: You are dead who were kicked out of the place your ancestors lie. The most powerful of ritualists are gifted the knowledge of how to return to the place where the dead reign.</li> <li>Effect: The ritualist opens an Avernian gate if one is currently present.\u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Common Ritual Factors:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Duration and Radius</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T17:20:25-08:00","id":1269698,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on the Blood Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T17:45:56-08:00","id":1280798,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>The Sanctum(Covenant)<ul><li>The city has been under siege for days. You haven\u2019t seen your brother since the Edomite arrived two weeks ago. At this point, it's just a cycle of death. You never thought it would happen. That bastard actually went to Rome. You hope to kill soon for his betrayal. You and the other men try to keep calm. Everyone has been on edge since Simeon disappeared a few nights ago. The only thing left where he stood guard was a blood tunic ripped to shreds, as if by a beast. No matter. It's a half moon tonight and you look up at it in amazement. From the corner of your eye, you see something. You turn to look and it's your brother wearing priestly garb. You smile and go to embrace him before you ask yourself the question, how did he get past Herod\u2019s soldiers. \u201cOh, my beloved kin. It is good that you embrace what is to come.\u201d you hear him say before you collapse to the ground.</li> <li>Where We Came From: On the eve of the death of King Yerav\u2019am, a group of Kindred met. Israelites and Judeans, monotheists and henotheists/monolatrists joined together in an alliance to reorganize their community. This disparate alliance was based on preserving a community that the elders and ancilla among them had seen ripped to shreds many times before and refused to permit to occur again. Simeon of Judah and Rivkah of Ephraim bound each of their childer with Vinculum and they bound their own childer. From then on they spread amongst the other afflicted in our midsts. Giving those who wished to weaken the whole Final Death.</li> <li>Our Practices: We are survivors. Banished from the embrace of Sheol and blessed with the gift of new covenants with our Lord. While we may be segmented, we are ultimately united. Across tribal, national, and faith we all recognize the importance of our callings. To be holy terrors. This takes a multiplicity of forms: from the zoneh who tortures and kills the unrighteous who defiles the Shabbat, to the diseased hermit who offers unholy insight.</li> <li>When We\u2019re In Power: It\u2019s the Wilderness, the reign of Saul and David, the regency of Athaliah, the Hasmonean Dynasty. The best times for us come in many forms. Whether it be punishing those who stray from G-d or consuming those with the gall to attempt to destroy us; or appreciating the sovereignty over the shadows we\u2019ve been promised.</li> <li>When We\u2019re In Trouble: Our people know adversity. We have been slaves and displaced many times before. We have seen persecution at the hands of those we protect and those we swear to destroy. We endure. Whether it be cycles of torpor or the encroachment of the goyim and the others that they bring. Through outright assaults, covert assassinations, induced torpor, and simply hiding we survive to fight another day.</li> <li>Sects:<ul><li>Shedim: The youngest and largest sect, they\u2019re predominately monotheists and those who never turned from El as their patron. This group has gone through a variety of changes in recent centuries: from originally being a cult centered around a secret priesthood dedicated solely to El to sages and mystics gleaning information for their community. The most scholarly of the sects that stalk the streets of ancient Judaea, these young and commonly zealous are never far from the center of religious and cultural conflicts.<ul><li>Beliefs: Our covenant is with Adonai. We reside on the level of Samael in separation to G-d and are charged with keeping our people in line and delving the depths of His secrets for eternity.</li> <li>Rituals and Observances:<ul><li>Mikvah of HaSatan - The newly embraced is taken on Rosh Chodesh to bathe in the blood and gore of the imperfect, blatant mockeries of the sin offerings.</li> <li>Lamadnu(To learn) - You are charged with deeply studying the nature of the blood and the Heavens.</li> <li>Taharah(Purity) - Those of the priestly castes are closer to G-d. As such those of them who come into our state are favored.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Rephites: Predominately elders and ancilla who barely survived the Assyrian and Babylonian captivities. The few members of this sect believe strongly in their callings and their covenant with Maweth and Resheph. Around the time of the King Josiah\u2019s reformation and the mass banning of other G-ds, their ranks have started to cultivate ghoul cults from the former Cults of Asherah, Anat, Qetesh, and others. They consider their counterparts to be heretics and keep to their traditional hermitage while teaching those who wish to learn.<ul><li>Beliefs: While El and Asherah are supreme, they are no longer our patrons. We serve Maweth and Resheph foremost, for our condition is a covenant with them.</li> <li>Rituals and Observances<ul><li>Mikvah at Gehenna - Each Yom Kippur they slaughter animals used in sin offerings and bathe in the gore.</li> <li>Kavod(Honor) - Do not come in contact with the Levites and Kohanim.</li> <li>Nekamah(Revenge) - Undermine those who threw out our G-ds.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Lilithian: The most secretive and smallest sect, they\u2019re also entirely female. The earliest members of the sect worshipped the owls, lilin. They spend much of their time in orgiastic rituals and tempting the weak-willed. During the night they go out and dance, tempting men and women alike with their sweet smells and seductive allure. From Samaria to the Negev they patrol, offering pleasure and death in equal spades.<ul><li>Beliefs: The Whore Mother promises retribution and freedom for those who take up her cause. We are under a new covenant with her. To cull the perverse so that the meek will inherit.</li> <li>Rituals and Observances<ul><li>Mikvah of the Zoneh - Each Yom Kippur they are charged with seducing someone who committed a heinous act against someone who was defenseless. These criminals are then killed brutally and the neonate must bathe in their gore.</li> <li>Mishpachah(Family) - A man may never be gifted with our powers and a sister is not to come to harm unless she betrays her own kind.</li> <li>Gehmul(Retribution) - Since the nights of the Wilderness, the initiates have been charged by their fell patrons to claim the line of those they visit justice on fully.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:49:22-07:00","id":1384557,"title":"","content":"I think this is the first Jewish Requiem thread I've ever seen that wasn't mostly narishkeit, I didn't even think that was possible. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24708_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24708\" data-vbnamecard=\"24708\">Spectre9924</a> I think you're the only person to ever make what I always felt was the fairly obvious Dammitic-Frankist connection. I am so into this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267502#post1267502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely! I was thinking about them being mostly Nosferatu and Gangrel with some Daeva and even less Mekhet(if any).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If we're talking about the period between the end of Egyptian captivity until the beginning of the Babylonian one, it makes perfect sense that Israelite kindred would fear and shun Mekhet. But my suspicion is that without <i>any </i>they'd have no means of effectively countering espionage and attempts at regime change by their former masters. What about a single bloodline, connected somehow with Moses' early life in the shadowy palace of the pharaoh. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1267502#post1267502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was going to have Hekhalot be a system like Theban to highlight the cultural and theological shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>check out the <i>Sefer HaRazim</i> for an IRL example of weaponized Hekhalot mysticism: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sefer_HaRazim\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sefer_HaRazim</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","name":"hermeskhthonios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:29:31-07:00","id":1384566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hermeskhthonios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384557#post1384557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is the first Jewish Requiem thread I've ever seen that wasn't mostly narishkeit, I didn't even think that was possible. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24708_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24708\" data-vbnamecard=\"24708\">Spectre9924</a> I think you're the only person to ever make what I always felt was the fairly obvious Dammitic-Frankist connection. I am so into this.<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> If we're talking about the period between the end of Egyptian captivity until the beginning of the Babylonian one, it makes perfect sense that Israelite kindred would fear and shun Mekhet. But my suspicion is that without <i>any </i>they'd have no means of effectively countering espionage and attempts at regime change by their former masters. What about a single bloodline, connected somehow with Moses' early life in the shadowy palace of the pharaoh.<br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> check out the <i>Sefer HaRazim</i> for an IRL example of weaponized Hekhalot mysticism: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sefer_HaRazim\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sefer_HaRazim</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! I'll check it out! Definitely! Especially with the time period that they entered the Sanctified it feels like they'd be the only ones who would realistically join. I need to start getting to whether or not medieval Jewish Kindred would likely organize in mystery cults or a covenant. I might create covenants for ones amongst Beta Israel and sizeable communities that could defend themselves relatively more effectively with mystery cult options for Christian, Zoroastrian, and Muslim dominated areas. I like the idea of a specific line of Mekhet who found their way amongst the Israelites. I was relatively worried about connections with Mekhet and Theban but it honestly would make sense for their to be loose similarities. I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T23:09:25-07:00","id":1384581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384566#post1384566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Especially with the time period that they entered the Sanctified it feels like they'd be the only ones who would realistically join.I</div> </div> </div> </div>After they got their rejection letters from Nathan of Gaza's Yeshiva ha-Tanninim, what other choice did they have? (a crypto-Sabbatean Yeshiva of the Dragons with the False Prophet himself as the Rav; how's <i>that</i> for a Jewish mystery cult tucked away in one of the big 5 covenants?)<br /> <br /> regarding similarities between &quot;Applied Hekhalot Theology&quot; (idk what to call it) and Theban Sorcery, my initial thought is that at the one or two dot level loose similarities can be the best method for underscoring the differences. One method could be to have some noticeable overlap in the <i>results </i>of a few rituals. like (for sake of argument) both disciplines have a two dot ritual that stops a target from using language of any sort until the next sunrise. but the hekhalot rite (in this case) is much more akin to calling in an airstrike: your angelic ally needs you to be present, laying eyes on the target, or else it will not agree to your request. the short, word-shattering trumpet blast will hit not only your main target but also up to two other people within a five foot radius of them. if there is no one, friend or foe, within that radius, the target makes two rolls to resist. if they fail both, they also lose the ability to process and comprehend complex sentences until the next sunrise, whether you want them to or not.<br /> <br /> i sort of made that up on the fly but i hope you see what i'm getting at. three dot rites should, as a rule, diverge more than just turning a sniper rifle into a sawed-off or vice versa. i'd assume by that point you wouldn't just be begging minor favors from the divine sentries and inventory-scribes of the Outer Palace","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","user":"hermeskhthonios","date":". 04-29-2020, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","name":"hermeskhthonios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:47:06-07:00","id":1384666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hermeskhthonios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384581#post1384581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After they got their rejection letters from Nathan of Gaza's Yeshiva ha-Tanninim, what other choice did they have? (a crypto-Sabbatean Yeshiva of the Dragons with the False Prophet himself as the Rav; how's <i>that</i> for a Jewish mystery cult tucked away in one of the big 5 covenants?)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love that idea and would like to possibly use it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hermeskhthonios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384581#post1384581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">regarding similarities between &quot;Applied Hekhalot Theology&quot; (idk what to call it) and Theban Sorcery, my initial thought is that at the one or two dot level loose similarities can be the best method for underscoring the differences. One method could be to have some noticeable overlap in the <i>results </i>of a few rituals. like (for sake of argument) both disciplines have a two dot ritual that stops a target from using language of any sort until the next sunrise. but the hekhalot rite (in this case) is much more akin to calling in an airstrike: your angelic ally needs you to be present, laying eyes on the target, or else it will not agree to your request. the short, word-shattering trumpet blast will hit not only your main target but also up to two other people within a five foot radius of them. if there is no one, friend or foe, within that radius, the target makes two rolls to resist. if they fail both, they also lose the ability to process and comprehend complex sentences until the next sunrise, whether you want them to or not.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel what you mean here and like it. I've used the Blood Sorcery rules presented in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a>s book Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation as a jumping point for where I plan on taking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T18:21:17-07:00","id":1384750,"title":"","content":"i would happily write it up for you if you're still into the idea when you get to the 17th century. I genuinely respect him as a person so I'd love crafting an undead occult science AU for him. Why <i>wait </i>for a bold and resolute Moshiach ben Yosef? Is not growing him in a vat of vitae a profound act of tikkun olam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","user":"hermeskhthonios","date":". 04-29-2020, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","name":"hermeskhthonios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T19:12:22-07:00","id":1384756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hermeskhthonios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384750#post1384750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i would happily write it up for you if you're still into the idea when you get to the 17th century. I genuinely respect him as a person so I'd love crafting an undead occult science AU for him. Why <i>wait </i>for a bold and resolute Moshiach ben Yosef? Is not growing him in a vat of vitae a profound act of tikkun olam?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be greatly appreciated, and I like the way I'm still working on meshing into the Middle Ages and trying to make things community-specific for example, I was thinking about making a Chassidish mystery cult for those living in Germany and a covenant for pre-Islamic Arabia. While we're at it, who says that the Moshiach is supposed to be found among the living at all? A dhampir could do the job, or possibly a Masquerade breaking sect who literally resurrects their faithful from the dead under the guise of being the followers of the messiah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T20:43:49-07:00","id":1384769,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. From the Babylonian Talmud onward there have been significant fluctuations of (both popular and rabbinic) opinion about the number of people HaShem would need to anoint as Moshiach during the final years of the world's redemption. I imagine that would be just as true of our undead coreligionists, but for them &quot;definitely just one&quot; would almost never be able to rally much enthusiasm. The laity are almost always strongly wedded to the idea of at least two messiahs, with one of them either coming from among the Kindred or perhaps needing to be Embraced in order for the great work of redemption to be completed. Most the major vampiric rabbinic thinkers have basically been of that opinion, but far far wordier in describing it. What do you think?<br /> <br /> EDIT: just to clarify the seating capacity here, IIRC four messiahs is as high as IRL Jewish theology has been willing to go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","user":"hermeskhthonios","date":". 04-30-2020, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24327-hermeskhthonios","name":"hermeskhthonios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T23:23:58-07:00","id":1384786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hermeskhthonios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1264984-semitic-covenants-and-blood-sorceries?p=1384769#post1384769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. From the Babylonian Talmud onward there have been significant fluctuations of (both popular and rabbinic) opinion about the number of people HaShem would need to anoint as Moshiach during the final years of the world's redemption. I imagine that would be just as true of our undead coreligionists, but for them &quot;definitely just one&quot; would almost never be able to rally much enthusiasm. The laity are almost always strongly wedded to the idea of at least two messiahs, with one of them either coming from among the Kindred or perhaps needing to be Embraced in order for the great work of redemption to be completed. Most the major vampiric rabbinic thinkers have basically been of that opinion, but far far wordier in describing it. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that a lot and it also reminds me of a mystery cult I've been fleshing out of supernatural(vampires, werewolves, mages) and mortals who specifically look to defend those who they suspect of being Lamed Vavniki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:23:25-07:00","id":1387408,"title":"","content":"Some of the Blood Sorcery so far: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1g4nMoSezFrb36ka7A9V8z5KxjAUQUytQ_p5eD1tKRMU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}